WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.373
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B one.

2
00:00:05.673 --> 00:00:09.199
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.499 --> 00:00:15.960
Unit twenty: Used to / Be used to / Get used to. Today you will distinguish past habits from things that are familiar.

4
00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:19.040
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.337
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.183 --> 00:00:25.184
Used to.

7
00:00:26.183 --> 00:00:30.157
Used to means a past habit that no longer exists.

8
00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:32.459
I used to live in Siem Reap.

9
00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:35.679
Your turn. Say: Used to.

10
00:00:38.533 --> 00:00:39.569
Used to.

11
00:00:40.317 --> 00:00:41.399
Be used to.

12
00:00:42.383 --> 00:00:44.894
Be used to means to be familiar with something.

13
00:00:45.483 --> 00:00:47.158
I am used to the heat.

14
00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:50.484
Your turn. Say: Be used to.

15
00:00:53.333 --> 00:00:54.543
Be used to.

16
00:00:55.283 --> 00:00:56.401
Get used to.

17
00:00:57.417 --> 00:00:59.973
Get used to means to become familiar with something.

18
00:01:00.583 --> 00:01:02.432
I'm getting used to my new school.

19
00:01:03.017 --> 00:01:05.762
Your turn. Say: Get used to.

20
00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:09.787
Get used to.

21
00:01:10.550 --> 00:01:11.354
Habit.

22
00:01:12.350 --> 00:01:14.826
Habit means something you do regularly.

23
00:01:15.417 --> 00:01:16.662
Running is a habit.

24
00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:19.647
Your turn. Say: Habit.

25
00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:23.269
Habit.

26
00:01:24.017 --> 00:01:25.076
Familiar.

27
00:01:26.083 --> 00:01:27.897
Familiar means well known to you.

28
00:01:28.483 --> 00:01:29.798
A familiar street.

29
00:01:30.383 --> 00:01:32.954
Your turn. Say: Familiar.

30
00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:36.650
Familiar.

31
00:01:37.417 --> 00:01:38.035
New.

32
00:01:39.050 --> 00:01:40.864
New means not known before.

33
00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:42.590
A new city.

34
00:01:43.183 --> 00:01:45.754
Your turn. Say: New.

35
00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:49.473
New.

36
00:01:50.217 --> 00:01:51.229
Strange.

37
00:01:52.217 --> 00:01:54.924
Strange means unusual or unfamiliar.

38
00:01:55.517 --> 00:01:56.866
Strange food.

39
00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:59.986
Your turn. Say: Strange.

40
00:02:02.833 --> 00:02:03.869
Strange.

41
00:02:04.617 --> 00:02:05.583
Adapt.

42
00:02:06.583 --> 00:02:09.477
Adapt means to change to fit a new situation.

43
00:02:10.083 --> 00:02:11.433
I adapt quickly.

44
00:02:12.017 --> 00:02:14.704
Your turn. Say: Adapt.

45
00:02:17.567 --> 00:02:18.417
Adapt.

46
00:02:19.233 --> 00:02:23.232
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:24.083 --> 00:02:26.687
Visal, what did you use to do as a child?

48
00:02:27.783 --> 00:02:38.112
I used to play outside every afternoon. Used to is for a past habit or state that is finished. It is followed by the base verb.

49
00:02:39.217 --> 00:02:40.520
And be used to?

50
00:02:41.617 --> 00:02:53.812
Be used to means familiar, and it is followed by a noun or -ing: I am used to getting up early. Get used to means become familiar: I am getting used to the new school.

51
00:02:54.917 --> 00:02:56.173
What is the negative?

52
00:02:57.283 --> 00:03:08.112
Didn't use to: I didn't use to like fish. With the other two we use the normal verb be or get: I'm not used to the cold. Do not mix the base verb with the -ing form.

53
00:03:09.267 --> 00:03:10.895
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:15.363
Grammar focus: Used to and be used to and get used to.

55
00:03:15.663 --> 00:03:16.815
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:17.517 --> 00:03:19.876
I used to play outside every afternoon.

57
00:03:20.783 --> 00:03:22.586
I am used to getting up early.

58
00:03:23.483 --> 00:03:25.506
I am getting used to my new school.

59
00:03:26.467 --> 00:03:32.706
Used to + base verb = past habit. Be / get used to + noun or -ing = familiar / becoming familiar.

60
00:03:33.450 --> 00:03:36.787
Be careful! Don't say: I am used to live here.

61
00:03:38.733 --> 00:03:41.012
Say: I am used to living here.

62
00:03:41.312 --> 00:03:43.172
Use -ing after be used to.

63
00:03:43.967 --> 00:03:46.898
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:49.467
Old Habits, New Places.

65
00:03:49.767 --> 00:03:53.125
As a child, I used to play outside every afternoon.

66
00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:56.725
Now I am used to getting up at six every day.

67
00:03:57.733 --> 00:04:01.173
At first the new school was strange, but I am getting used to it.

68
00:04:02.167 --> 00:04:04.712
A new city is not familiar at first.

69
00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:07.990
People adapt when they live somewhere new.

70
00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:13.322
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:14.183 --> 00:04:17.367
I blank live in a village, but now I live in a city.

72
00:04:17.667 --> 00:04:21.460
A, used to. B, am used to. C, get used to.

73
00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:26.860
The answer is A: used to.

74
00:04:28.017 --> 00:04:29.471
I'm blank the noise now.

75
00:04:29.771 --> 00:04:33.366
A, used to. B, use to. C, used.

76
00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:38.946
The answer is A: used to.

77
00:04:40.083 --> 00:04:41.317
Which is correct?

78
00:04:41.617 --> 00:04:47.847
A, I am used to wake up early.. B, I am used to waking up early.. C, I used to waking up early..

79
00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:54.502
The answer is B: I am used to waking up early..

80
00:04:55.650 --> 00:04:57.115
'Get used to' means blank.

81
00:04:57.415 --> 00:05:02.183
A, become familiar. B, stop doing. C, remember.

82
00:05:05.733 --> 00:05:08.012
The answer is A: become familiar.

83
00:05:09.150 --> 00:05:12.566
According to the reading, what did the writer do as a child?

84
00:05:12.866 --> 00:05:17.251
A, played outside. B, studied late. C, travelled abroad.

85
00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:22.927
The answer is A: played outside.

86
00:05:24.133 --> 00:05:27.680
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:28.517 --> 00:05:30.656
What have you had to get used to recently?

88
00:05:39.450 --> 00:05:40.927
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:41.227 --> 00:05:52.590
Recently I have had to get used to waking up at five thirty because my new school starts early. I used to wake up at seven. Now I am used to it, and I feel more energetic.

90
00:05:52.890 --> 00:05:54.610
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:55.517 --> 00:06:00.863
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and used to and be used to and get used to.

92
00:06:01.163 --> 00:06:05.440
Today's value is perseverance. Keep trying, even when it is hard.

93
00:06:05.740 --> 00:06:08.288
See you in Unit twenty-one. Goodbye!

94
00:06:08.588 --> 00:06:11.020
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

